{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "החודש הזה", :translit "ha-chodesh ha-zeh", :gloss "this month"} {:he "חודש", :translit "chodesh", :gloss "month"} {:he "באחד בניסן ר\"ה למלכים ולרגלים ולחדשים", :translit "be-echad be-nisan r\"h la-melachim u-la-regalim u-la-chodashim", :gloss "on the first of Nisan is the New Year for kings, for festivals, and for months"} {:he "חדש", :translit "chadesh", :gloss "new / renew"} {:he "לרגלים", :translit "la-regalim", :gloss "for festivals"} {:he "לכם", :translit "lachem", :gloss "to you"} {:he "מלך", :translit "melech", :gloss "king"} {:he "ניסן", :translit "nisan", :gloss "Nisan"} {:he "למלכים", :translit "la-melachim", :gloss "for kings"} {:he "חדשי חדשים", :translit "chodshei chodashim", :gloss "months of months"} {:he "שבעה עולים לעיבור השנה", :translit "shivah olim le-ibbur ha-shanah", :gloss "seven who ascend for intercalation of the year"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["חודש" "חודש" "חודש"]} {:kind :gematria, :a "חדש", :b "לרגלים"} {:kind :gematria, :a "ניסן", :b "למלכים"} {:kind :other, :note "לכם is an anagram of מלך"} {:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["חודש"]} {:kind :other, :note "Removing 3 instances of חודש from the verse leaves 7 words, matching the 7 judges for intercalation"}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah teaches that on the first of Nisan is the New Year for kings, festivals, and months (Mishnah Rosh HaShanah 1:1). The Gemara elaborates that the first of Nisan is the New Year for kings, for festivals, and for the rental of houses (Rosh HaShanah 2a–b, parallel to Mishnah Rosh HaShanah 1:1). Regarding intercalation, the Mishnah states that they do not intercalate a year with fewer than seven judges (Sanhedrin 2a, Mishnah Sanhedrin 1:2).", :sources ["Mishnah Rosh HaShanah 1:1" "Rosh HaShanah 2a" "Mishnah Sanhedrin 1:2" "Sanhedrin 2a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ראשון הוא לכם", :translit "rishon hu lachem", :gloss "it is first for you"} {:he "דברו", :translit "dabru", :gloss "you shall speak"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word דברו adjacent to ראשון הוא לכם signals that sanctification of the new month requires the Great Sanhedrin to speak it"}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah states that the sanctification of the new month is performed by the Great Sanhedrin (Mishnah Rosh HaShanah 2:1, Sanhedrin 2b). The adjacency of 'דברו' to 'ראשון הוא לכם' links the requirement of the court's verbal declaration to this verse.", :sources ["Mishnah Rosh HaShanah 2:1" "Sanhedrin 2b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לחדשי השנה", :translit "le-chodshei ha-shanah", :gloss "for the months of the year"} {:he "עולת חודש בחדשו לחדשי השנה", :translit "olat chodesh be-chadsho le-chodshei ha-shanah", :gloss "the burnt offering of the month in its month for the months of the year"} {:he "חדש והבא קרבן מתרומה חדשה", :translit "chodesh ve-hava korb mi-terumah chadashah", :gloss "a new month and its offering from new terumah"} {:he "ראשון הוא לכם לחדשי השנה", :translit "rishon hu lachem le-chodshei ha-shanah", :gloss "it is first for you for the months of the year"} {:he "ניסן", :translit "nisan", :gloss "Nisan"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לחדשי השנה" "לחדשי השנה"]}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah lists the first of Nisan as the New Year for tithes of cattle and for the counting of the months (Mishnah Rosh HaShanah 1:1). The Tosefta (Menachot 6:1) states that all communal offerings from the first of Nisan onward come from the new terumah collection, deriving this from the verse's language of 'the first for you for the months of the year.' The phrase 'a new month and its offering comes from new terumah' is the halakhic principle recorded in the Tosefta (Menachot 6:1).", :sources ["Mishnah Rosh HaShanah 1:1" "Tosefta Menachot 6:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["חודש" "חודש" "חודש"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "חודש", :refs ["Genesis 29:14" "Exodus 1:8" "Exodus 23:15" "Exodus 34:18" "Leviticus 26:10" "Leviticus 27:6" "Numbers 3:15" "Numbers 3:22"], :n 67, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "חודש", :refs ["Genesis 29:14" "Exodus 1:8" "Exodus 23:15" "Exodus 34:18" "Leviticus 26:10" "Leviticus 27:6" "Numbers 3:15" "Numbers 3:22"], :n 67, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "חודש", :refs ["Genesis 29:14" "Exodus 1:8" "Exodus 23:15" "Exodus 34:18" "Leviticus 26:10" "Leviticus 27:6" "Numbers 3:15" "Numbers 3:22"], :n 67, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:a-value 312, :b-value 313, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "לרגלים", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "חדש"} {:kind :gematria, :a "ניסן", :a-value 170, :b "למלכים", :b-value 170, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "לכם is an anagram of מלך", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["חודש"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "חודש", :refs ["Genesis 29:14" "Exodus 1:8" "Exodus 23:15" "Exodus 34:18" "Leviticus 26:10" "Leviticus 27:6" "Numbers 3:15" "Numbers 3:22"], :n 67, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "Removing 3 instances of חודש from the verse leaves 7 words, matching the 7 judges for intercalation", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Word דברו adjacent to ראשון הוא לכם signals that sanctification of the new month requires the Great Sanhedrin to speak it", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לחדשי השנה" "לחדשי השנה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "לחדשי השנה", :refs ["Exodus 12:2" "Numbers 28:14"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "לחדשי השנה", :refs ["Exodus 12:2" "Numbers 28:14"], :n 2, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:15:13.789576996Z", :model "glm-5.2"}